  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Special Climate Change Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The activities of the Special Climate Change Fund include capacity building and technical assistance to SIDS governments in the following areas: addressing water stress due to sea-level rise, climate resilience across coastal ecosystems and infrastructure and in agriculture and food systems. Interventions will also address human security and livelihoods. In line with Ireland&#x2019;s climate policy priorities on adaptation and a focus on Least Developed Countries and Small Island Developing States, the SCCF has identified a significant gap in the global climate finance architecture: specific support for Small Island Developing States, particularly those that are not Least Developed Countries &#x2013; which are struggling to access international climate funds for adaptation projects.</narrative>
  </description>
